# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# proptest failure-seed persistence. Not committed: the only seeds generated so far
# are RED-proof residue (inputs that failed under deliberately-injected, reverted
# bugs — not real regressions of shipped code). A genuine future failure is caught
# by CI and its minimal input logged in the run output, so replay persistence is
# not relied upon here. Two forms: unit tests write a proptest-regressions/ DIR;
# integration tests (tests/) write a <name>.proptest-regressions FILE.
**/proptest-regressions/
*.proptest-regressions

